# di_same_name_cross_ns.tkr — a NAMESPACE-IDENTITY project-regressor (0.3.1
# regressor-principal, §5 triage exception): two DI providers/contracts sharing the SAME bare
# name (`Face`/`Svc`) in DIFFERENT namespaces (`left`/`right`) must resolve independently
# (issue #284). Flattening into one snippet would either collide the two same-bare types or
# remove the namespace distinction the DI keying under test depends on. Kept on disk,
# unflattened; not inline-scenario-izable.

#
# UNFOLD (2026-07-26, owner ruling "está proibido inline code em tkr"): this project is also a HOST
# for scenarios that used to be `Given source inline` blocks in regressor.tkr. Each is a MEMBER
# NAMESPACE under `src/`, selected by `TEKO_REGR_ENTRY`, and every one of them runs off THIS
# project's SINGLE build — the runner compiles a project's `.tkp` at most once per `.tkr`
# (`RegrBuilt`), and the members differ only by the env selector, args and stdin, never by source.
# The project's own scenario is unchanged and still runs from the same binary with no selector set.

Feature: di_same_name_cross_ns — same-bare-name DI providers stay keyed by canonical namespace

  Scenario: left::Svc and right::Svc, sharing the bare name Svc, each inject their own namespace's Face
    When built and run
    Then exit = 42

