Feature: F9 romaneio .31 — the audit's positive regressions (backend x scenario) (unfolded from regressor.tkr — members of this project's single build)

  # (B-S1) The own backend coerces into a null-union at EVERY placement that declares a type, not
  # only at the binding: `x = null` after a `T | null` binding used to write a raw `const 0` into the
  # VReg the `match` then reads as the wrapper's base address — a load from address 0. The `c` rows
  # are the differential control: the C backend wrapped at the assign all along.

  Scenario: d1_cast_pair_parity_between_arith_and_compare
    Given env = ["TEKO_REGR_ENTRY=q186_d1_cast_pair_parity_between_arith_and"]
    When built and run
    Then exit = 42

  # (B-S3) The LEGITIMATE `ref` forward — same referent type — keeps compiling. It is the case the
  # original wagon shipped without a fixture, which is why the missing `type_eq` went unnoticed.
